---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import BrainFlipCard from '../components/BrainFlipCard.astro';
import { NN_BRAIN_MAPPINGS } from '../lib/nn-brain-map';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Prototype It To Explain Itself"
  description="Teaching analogies that pair neural-network architectures with brain-inspired metaphors. Flip the cards to compare sides."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl not-prose">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4 text-zinc-900">
      Different networks, different teaching analogies
    </h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      A convolutional net does not do what a transformer does. Each architecture is built for a
      different kind of input and a different kind of output. To make that stick, each card pairs
      the network with a <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-800">brain-inspired metaphor</strong>
      — a teaching aid, not a biology lesson.
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Tap a card to flip between the <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-800">network side</strong>
      and the <strong class="font-medium text-zinc-800">analogy side</strong>. Multimodal systems
      stitch several of these together — vision here, language there — because no single network
      covers every data type.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-10">
      {NN_BRAIN_MAPPINGS.map((mapping) => (
        <BrainFlipCard mapping={mapping} />
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mb-10">
      Analogies inspired by public lecture framing. None of these pairings claim to describe how the brain actually works.
    </p>

    <div class="p-6 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-3xl shadow-sm">
      <div class="font-medium mb-2 text-zinc-900">Go deeper</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mb-4">
        The <a href="/concepts" class="underline hover:text-zinc-900">concepts index</a> links each
        mapping to working demos and reference pages in this repo. The
        <a href="/reflect-and-attempt-quizz.html" class="underline hover:text-zinc-900">Reflect and Attempt Quizz</a>
        tests what you picked up.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/concepts"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 px-4 py-2 bg-white border border-zinc-300 text-zinc-800 hover:bg-zinc-100 hover:border-zinc-400 rounded-2xl text-sm font-medium"
        >
          All concepts <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/reflect-and-attempt-quizz.html"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 px-4 py-2 bg-white border border-zinc-300 text-zinc-800 hover:bg-zinc-100 hover:border-zinc-400 rounded-2xl text-sm font-medium"
        >
          Open the tester <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
